- supported the development of the sampling design, questionnaire and  counting rule for  data, .
- supported the development of materials on forced labour and child labour
- supported the Judiciary and Legal Training Institute to develop the manual and conduct a Training of Trainers 
- supported the Malaysian Employers Federation (MEF) to develop the employers guide and training manual and conduct a Training of Trainers with the MEF Academy
- supported the assessment of referral systems on forced labour and human trafficking, and develop a guide 
- supported the Malaysian Anti-Trafficking in Persons and Smuggling of Migrants Council to develop a manual for enforcement agencies, and an e-learning tool
- supported the MTUC to conduct awareness raising events on forced labour and develop materials  
- collaborated with the Ministry of Human Resources, Human Rights Commission of Malaysia to promote the Call for Pledges against child labour.
